description.narrative:
To ensure a world of work free from violence and harassment for all, a new Law No. 12 of 2022 on sexual harassment has been adopted, and a Ministerial Decree No. 88 of 2023 concerning prevention and handling sexual harassment at the workplace, guides,   and training manual on addressing violence and harassment at the workplace for workers and employers has been issued. 
At least five policies at the enterprise level have been developed in the palm oil sector since 2022. The ILO through  funding from RBSA and the Government of the United States mainly supported interventions, advocacy, and promotion of C190 and R206 led to the following:
- policy input to Ministry of Manpower Regulation on Guidelines to address Violence and Harassment at the Workplace, and policy discussion for Formulation of Government Regulation's Working Group in response to Law No. 12 Year 2022 on Sexual Crime Act and Ministerial Decree No. 88 of 2023
- capacity building and training to local provincial governments (in collaboration with the Ministry of Manpower), employers associations and companies, and workers based on the developed Guideline on Addressing Violence and Harassment in the World of Work and the ILO/UN Women training module;
- supporting discussion, consultations, and training on the prevention of violence and harassment in certain sectors of work, namely maritime, palm oil, fishing processing, media & journalistic; especially for women. This has been done not only at the national level but also in many provinces and districts;
- More than 100,000 people were reached from awareness campaign messages through offline and online activities.  Conducted the first online survey on violence and harassment in the world of work in Indonesia;
- Supporting employer association (APINDO) in FGD consultations, formulation, and launching of the renewal of the Employers' Guide on Prevention of Sexual Harassment at the Workplace;
- Training workshops to build the capacity of tripartite constituents to better understand the prevalence of online violence and harassment, and discuss recommendations and possible ways forward.
